  "slug": "genome-animals-f087",
  "summary": "Recent comparative analyses across 154 animal and 94 mammal species link gene content shifts and recombination suppression to evolutionary outcomes.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is comparative genomics across many species, linking specific genomic features to evolutionary outcomes. Ancestral reconstruction across 154 animal genomes spanning 11 land-colonization events reports convergent patterns of gene gain and loss associated with the emergence of terrestrial animals. Separately, deep learning on 22 mammal genome alignments maps an X-linked recombination desert, described as an ancient speciation supergene across 94 species. A distinct transcriptomic study of 14 murine multilayered epithelia reports a conserved p63-Notch axis governing basal identity and suprabasal commitment. What is new is the taxonomic breadth and the explicit linkage of gene content shifts and recombination suppression to evolutionary outcomes.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-18"
}
